  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nitrous acid gives nitrosonium ion as electrophile&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>NO</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>)&nbsp;which attacks phenol at less hindered p-position of form p-nitrosophenol.&nbsp; The nitroso group undergo reduction and forms amine in the presence of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>SH</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bec81fab-2ffa-4d87-9b53-ba3853458d09.png\" style=\"width: 613px; height: 112px;\" /></p>",
